# Repo Workflow

This is the **Civic Lab** high-fidelity prototype: a React/Vite + Express app for a
thread-first Canon / Country Manuals knowledge system.

## Documents (different jobs)

| Artifact | Job |
|---|---|
| `CONCEPT.md` | General reference — product vision and vocabulary |
| `PLANNING.md` | Planning & coordination — milestones, sequencing, status board |
| `OPEN_ISSUES.md` | Current open work items + acceptance criteria |
| `SCRATCHPAD.json` | Agent session snapshot (focus / next step) |
| `src/` / `server/` / `db/` | Implementation |

See the **project-state** rule for write cadences and how the three continuity files
overlap without replacing each other.

## Stack (orient quickly)

- **Client:** React 19, React Router, Vite, Tailwind, Plate/Slate editor, MUI/Radix UI
- **Server:** Express + `tsx`, JSON files in `db/`
- **Package manager:** `pnpm` (lockfile present); `pnpm run dev` runs Vite + API

## Divergence protocol

Never let the prototype and `CONCEPT.md` diverge silently. When an implementation choice
improves on or contradicts the concept:

1. Implement it (if justified), and
2. Record the mismatch as an `OPEN_ISSUES.md` entry (and/or update `CONCEPT.md` if the
   user asked for a concept change). Plan any phased rollout in `PLANNING.md`.
